
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Host power/wake regressions (Windows, Visual C++ build tools required):

  pwsh -File test\host\run.ps1

These compile the real main.cpp and Heltec display adapter against hardware
mocks. Cases cover fast and fallback wake in both directions, book boundaries,
cold boot, awake navigation, sleep deadlines, framebuffer bytes and transaction
counts, and peripheral power-off/hold release. Executables are built in a
temporary directory and removed afterwards.
Battery tests cover the estimated Li-ion curve, sampling immediately on boot,
discarding the first conversion, trimmed-mean outlier rejection, sample caching,
invalid voltage handling and retry recovery.

Firmware compile checks:

  pio run -e vision-master-e213 -e crowpanel-e213

Hardware checks after flashing the Heltec target:
- Check cold boot, menu/upload, and next/previous navigation.
- Confirm reading and menu sleep after one minute without button activity.
- Press next/previous just before the deadline, including at book boundaries,
  and confirm each press grants another full minute awake.
- Check several consecutive sleep/wake cycles for ghosting or missing text.
- Compare battery-supply sleep current and button-to-page latency with the
  previous firmware. Host tests cannot measure these or validate panel timing.
